max-visits: 1
on-arrival: president = "Großmann"; president_party = "I"; social_fascism_adopted = 0; left_dissent = 5; unions_independent = 0; left_split = 0; reformists_resign = 0; centrists_resign = 0; center_dissent = 0; labor_dissent = 5; reformist_dissent = 5; spd_party_leader = "Wels"

= Our death is nearer than it seems.

On the morning of January of 17th, Gustav Noske has walked outside of his residency, this time around without any guards. In the peaceful times it would not really threaten President's life, however in the current prospect...

Noske has been fatally shot twenty times by unknown three assailants. Their identities have been covered and investigation has been trailed off by unknown elements: Likely they are sympathizers of the burgerblock alliance, who have recently turned against us.

With his death, social patriots and nationalists within party have lost considerably lot of power and have been ousted from their position by socialists, who in their turn have restored leftists in their position. Otto Wels assumed the new position of radical opposition against social fascists and the past history of SPD with Noske. He declared that republic can no longer be governed through peaceful means with such powerful reaction from right.

**Social Fascism** is dead.

- @root: Good riddance.
